        "min_height": 520,
        "background": "sand",
        "heading": "Carat: weight, not size",
        "text": "<p>Carat is weight. 100 points make one carat, so a quarter-carat stone is 25 points or 0.25ct.</p><p>Price jumps at the round numbers. A 0.90ct stone looks almost the same as a 1.00ct stone on the hand and costs noticeably less.</p>"
      }
